# Long shell commands

## Do not

- Pipe a long command into `tail`/`head` in the same Shell call when you need to wait for completion (`make test-integration 2>&1 | tail -40` buffers stdout, loses the exit code, wastes `block_until_ms`).
- Re-wait the same command if the user says it already finished — read the terminal file.
- Use `block_until_ms: 30000` for `make test-integration`, `make test-e2e`, `make test-manual`, or `docker compose up --wait` without backgrounding.

## Patterns

### 1. Short summary after completion (preferred)

```bash
LOG=/tmp/lateness-test-integration.log
make test-integration >"$LOG" 2>&1; ec=$?
echo "exit_code=$ec"
tail -n 40 "$LOG"
exit $ec
```

One Shell call, generous `block_until_ms` (see table), exit code preserved.

### 2. Background + terminal file

- `block_until_ms: 0` → background.
- Read `terminals/<id>.txt` (footer `exit_code` / `last_exit_code`).
- Poll with Await + a pattern (`exit_code:|FAIL|PASS|ok\\s+`) or re-read the terminal. Do not block forever with no pattern.

### 3. User already ran the command

- Read `terminals/*.txt` first.
- Do not re-run `make test-integration` if you only need to interpret the result.

## `block_until_ms` guide

| Command | Minimum |
|---|---|
| `make test-integration` | 300000 |
| `make test-e2e` | 300000 |
| `make test-manual` | 600000 |
| `make dev-up` (image build) | 300000 |
| `make validate`, `go test ./... -short` | 120000 |

When unsure — background (pattern 2) or a log file (pattern 1).

## Report to the user

Include the command, `exit_code`, and what you inspected (log tail or terminal file).
